cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the SIL paper below."
title: "SIL: Symbiotic Interactive Learning for Language-Conditioned Human-Agent Co-Adaptation"
abstract: >-
  SIL is a bidirectional co-adaptation framework in which both the human and the
  embodied agent maintain joint belief states in a shared latent task space that
  evolve with the interaction history, enabling proactive clarification, adaptive
  suggestions, and shared plan refinement. It couples foundation models for
  spatial perception and reasoning with a triplet-loss-trained neural encoder,
  and uses episodic / semantic memory regularised via elastic weight
  consolidation to mitigate catastrophic forgetting.
type: software
